there's all kind of chaos and  uncertainty across global markets but  bitcoin's price has been grinding up  higher and higher so let's take a look  at what's been going on this past week  first if we look at the bitcoin market  you can see that we're trading around 46  500  that's outperforming most of their  assets over the past week if we then  take a look at the bitcoin network  itself what we can see is that the  bitcoin market cap is just under 900  billion dollars now about 90 of the  supply has been issued and the 19th  million bitcoin has now officially been  put into circulation the real exchange  volume is 1.98 billion dollars and  miners were paid 42.5 million dollars  over the last 24 hours to continue to  secure bitcoin the most secure computing  network in the world bitcoin is also  trading at 40 up from the cycle low but  bitcoin has only ever been 210 days  higher than the current price point so  for over 95 of bitcoin's life it was at  a lower price point this is important  because if you continue to dollar cost  average you're probably in a pretty good  position if we then take a look at the  compound annual growth rate what we can  see is that bitcoin's 10-year compound  annual growth rate is 150 percent that  is destroying anything including the s p  which is only twelve point four percent  or the nasdaq at sixteen point six  percent bitcoin continues to compound at  an incredible pace and it doesn't have  any signs of slowing down anytime soon  now if we take a look at on chain  metrics we'll go to will clemente and  the blockwear team they put together  some great charts this week on it first  we see the short-term holdered realized  price we're just above it but according  to will we're gonna have to see another  day or two of closing above this level  that short term holder realized price  it's important to trade above it we're  there now but let's see if it holds then  if we go ahead and we take a look at the  next chart what we can see is that the  luna bitcoin holdings now as a reminder  luna has the ust which is a stable coin  they're backing it with bitcoin and you  can see here in this green line that  they continue to stack more and more  bitcoin they have three billion dollars  in reserves they're going to convert  into bitcoin with a goal of eventually  reaching 10 billion dollars in bitcoin  any time that you have a persistent  buyer in the billions of dollars coming  into the market of course the price is  going to be positively impacted and what  you can see is pretty much as soon as  they started to buy that price started  to skyrocket upwards if we then take a  look at the bitcoin balance on exchanges  what we can see is this green line  falling off a cliff since early march  that shows that people who had bitcoin  on exchanges who had recently bought it  they actually are moving it now taking  it off that exchange into self-custody  or cold storage that's a great sign for  bitcoin bulls because what it means is  that there's less bitcoin on the  exchange that simply in a couple of  clicks could be sold into the market  less cell pressure on the market  obviously means that the price is likely  to be bullish if we then go ahead and we  take a look at the otc desk holdings as  well we can see that they have fallen  off a cliff as well this is just another  signal showing that there is low cell  pressure meaning that the bulls are in  control the price continues to grind  upwards and every single data point we  have shows that it's likely to continue  and then last but not least if we take a  look at that illiquid supply shock ratio  we can see that that is ticked up  aggressively in the last week that green  line climbing towards the moon what this  tells us is that more and more and more  people are holding bitcoin they're not  willing to sell it over 70 percent of  bitcoin has not been sold in the last  year that's in circulation that's a big  deal because when you have a persistent  buyer like luna or even microstrategy  with their brand new 205 million dollar  loan that they took from silvergate  against their bitcoin collateral that's  hundreds of millions or billions of  dollars pouring into a market that's  highly illiquid that usually spells for  a bullish outlook  then lastly if we shift to the macro  environment we can see dylan leclair  pointing out that officially the 10 and  two year yield curves have officially  inverted once you get this inversion  historically it signals that there is a  recession that is looming now that  recession doesn't usually happen right  away it can take anywhere from six to 18  months to actually go ahead and play out  in some cases it happens on the shorter  end on other cases it happens over a  longer period of time but any time you  get a yield curve inversion you have to  start asking yourself where is the  recession going to come from when is it  going to happen ultimately this yield  curve inversion tells us one thing  people are going to be seeking safety  and regardless of whether wall street  treats bitcoin as a risk asset or not  the everyday average person they treat  bitcoin as their reserve asset they  continue to dollar cost average we have  an illiquid market there's plenty of  persistent buyers the price is grinding  up and even with a recession potentially  looming six to 18 months away  bitcoin looks not only healthy but it  looks like we're poised for a move  higher i hope that you enjoy these  breakdowns every single week next week  i'll be back with will clemente from  blockwear if you don't go follow him on  twitter go follow dylan and we'll be  back next saturday
 

